{
    "content2": {
      "content": "🧠 1. What Is Null Safety?",
      "type": "heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content3": {
      "content": "💡 Simple Definition:",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content4": {
      "content": "Null Safety means protecting your app from null (empty or uninitialized) values that can crash your code.",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content5": {
      "content": "🛑 Problem Before Null Safety:",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content6": {
      "content": "string name;\nprint(name.length); // ❌ error! name is not initialized",
      "type": "code",
      "typeOf": "code"
    },
    "content7": {
      "content": "Without null safety, accessing `.length` of a `null` value causes your app to crash.",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content8": {
      "content": "✅ Solution: Null Safety in Dart",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content9": {
      "content": "Dart ensures that **non-nullable variables must always have a value** before you use them.",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content33": {
      "content": "break",
      "type": "break",
      "typeOf": "break"
    },
    "content10": {
      "content": "🛒 Real-World Analogy:",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content":{
        "content":"Imagine a shopping cart:",
        "type":"paragraph",
        "typeOf":"Text"
    },
    "content11": {
      "content": "You must add items before checking out.\nIf the cart is empty (null), you can't proceed — just like you can't call `.length` on a null variable.",
      "type": "points",
      "typeOf": "List"
    },
    "content12": {
      "content": "✍️ Basic Syntax",
      "type": "heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content13": {
      "content": "🔒 Non-nullable variable (must always hold a value)",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content14": {
      "content": "string name = \"Alice\"; // ✅ must be initialized",
      "type": "code",
      "typeOf": "code"
    },
    "content15": {
      "content": "❓ Nullable variable (can be null, use `?`)",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content16": {
      "content": "string? name = null; // ✅ can be null",
      "type": "code",
      "typeOf": "code"
    },
    "content17": {
      "content": "✅ Access safely using null check",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content18": {
      "content": "if (name != null) {\n  print(name.length);\n}",
      "type": "code",
      "typeOf": "code"
    },
    "content19": {
      "content": "🪄 Null-aware operator (`?.`)",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content20": {
      "content": "print(name?.length); // Only runs if name is not null",
      "type": "code",
      "typeOf": "code"
    },
    "content21": {
      "content": "🧙 Null-coalescing operator (`??`)",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content22": {
      "content": "string username = name ?? \"Guest\"; // If name is null, use \"Guest\"",
      "type": "code",
      "typeOf": "code"
    },
    "content34": {
      "content": "break",
      "type": "break",
      "typeOf": "break"
    },
    "content23": {
      "content": "🔨 Step-by-Step Example",
      "type": "heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content24": {
      "content": "🎯 Use Case: Display a user's name, or show \"Guest\" if it's null.",
      "type": "sub-heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content25": {
      "content": "void main() {\n  string? userName; // Nullable variable\n\n  // Print length only if not null\n  print(\"User length: ${userName?.length}\");\n\n  // Use default value if null\n  string displayName = userName ?? \"Guest\";\n  print(\"Welcome, $displayName!\");\n}",
      "type": "code",
      "typeOf": "code"
    },
