    "content27": {
      "content": "✅ 5. Best Practices",
      "type": "heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content28": {
      "content": "Use non-nullable types by default\nUse nullable types only when a value can truly be absent\nUse `late` when you know a value **will** be set later\nUse `?`, `??`, `!`, `.length`, `.isEmpty`, etc. with care",
      "type": "points",
      "typeOf": "List"
    },
    "content36": {
      "content": "break",
      "type": "break",
      "typeOf": "break"
    },
    "content29": {
      "content": "📌 6. Key Takeaways",
      "type": "heading",
      "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content30": {
      "content": "Null safety makes your code safer and crash-free.\nUse `?` for nullable types.\nUse `?.`, `??`, and null checks (`if`) to safely access nullable variables.\nDart forces you to think about null — making your apps more reliable.",
      "type": "points",
      "typeOf": "List"
    },
